  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef works in a similar way to a travelling salesman ― he always travels to new cities in order to sell his delicious dishes.\n\nToday, Chef is planning to visit NNN cities (numbered 111 through NNN). There is a direct way to travel between each pair of cities. Each city has a specific temperature; let's denote the temperature in the iii-th city by CiC_iCi​. Chef has a fixed temperature tolerance DDD with the following meaning: for each pair of cities aaa and bbb, he may travel from city aaa directly to city bbb only if ∣Ca−Cb∣≤D|C_a-C_b| \\le D∣Ca​−Cb​∣≤D, otherwise he would catch a heavy flu because of the sudden change in temperature.\n\nChef starts from city 111. Is he able to visit all NNN cities in such a way that each city is visited **exactly once**?\n\nNotes:\n\n\nChef is not able to travel through a city without visiting it.\nCity 111 is visited at the beginning.\nIt is not necessary to be able to travel directly to city 111 from the last city Chef visits.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\le N \\le 10^52≤N≤105",
      "0≤D≤1090 \\le D \\le 10^90≤D≤109",
      "0≤Ci≤1090 \\le C_i \\le 10^90≤Ci​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):**",
      "N≤1,000N \\le 1,000N≤1,000",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10,00010,00010,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and DDD.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing the string `\"YES\"` (without quotes) if Chef can visit all cities or `\"NO\"` (without quotes) if he cannot.",
    "notes": [],
